  "response": "```python\ndef simulate_snake(board_size, snake, food, moves):\n    \"\"\"\n    Simulate a Snake game based on given board, snake state, food, and moves.\n\n    Args:\n        board_size: Tuple of (width, height)\n        snake: List of (x, y) tuples with head first\n        food: List of (x, y) tuples, only the first is active\n        moves: List of move directions (\"UP\", \"DOWN\", \"LEFT\", \"RIGHT\")\n\n    Returns:\n        Tuple of (final_snake, alive, food_eaten_count)\n    \"\"\"\n    width, height = board_size\n    \n    # Helper to check if a position is valid on the board\n    def is_valid_pos(x, y):\n        return 0 <= x < width and 0 <= y < height\n    \n    # Get current active food (first item in list, or None)\n    def get_active_food():\n        return food[0] if food else None\n    \n    # Check for collision with snake body (including head position of previous state)\n    def has_body_collision(new_head_x, new_head_y, moving):\n        current_snake = list(snake)  # copy to not modify in-place\n        # Don't count tail if it's about to move away and we're not growing\n        if not moving:\n            return False\n        # Check all body segments including head (excluding position of tail that may move away)\n        for i, seg in enumerate(snake):\n            # Tail segment: only exclude if not growing and it would move away\n            if i == len(snake) - 1 and not moving:\n                continue\n            if new_head_x, new_head_y == seg:\n                return True\n        return False\n\n    # Simulate one step of snake movement\n    def move_snake(direction, eat_food):\n        head_x, head_y = snake[0]\n        \n        # Determine new head position based on direction\n        if direction == \"UP\":\n            new_head_x, new_head_y = head_x, head_y - 1\n        elif direction == \"DOWN\":\n            new_head_x, new_head_y = head_x, head_y + 1\n        elif direction == \"LEFT\":\n            new_head_x, new_head_y = head_x - 1, head_y\n        elif direction == \"RIGHT\":\n            new_head_x, new_head_y = head_x + 1, head_y\n        \n        # Check for out-of-bounds or self-collision\n        if not is_valid_pos(new_head_x, new_head_y):\n            return None  # Snake died\n        if has_body_collision(new_head_x, new_head_y, eat_food):\n            return None  # Self-collision (including eating into own tail)\n        \n        # Apply movement: head moves to new position, body follows\n        # If not growing, remove last segment (tail)\n        new_snake = [(new_head_x, new_head_y)] + snake[:-1]\n        \n        # If eating food and there's food, grow by keeping tail in place\n        if eat_food:\n            current_food = get_active_food()\n            new_snake.append(current_food)  # Keep current length + 1\n            if current_food:\n                food.pop(0)  # Remove eaten food\n                if food:\n                    food.insert(0, food[-1])  # Shift active food to front (not needed but for clarity)\n        \n        return new_snake\n    \n    alive = True\n    food_eaten_count = 0\n    moving = False\n    \n    current_food_idx = 0\n    \n    # Get initial direction from head position and first body segment\n    if len(snake) > 1:\n        dx = snake[0][0] - snake[1][0]\n        dy = snake[0][1] - snake[1][1]\n        \n        if dx == 1:\n            moving = \"RIGHT\"\n        elif dx == -1:\n            moving = \"LEFT\"\n        elif dy == 1:\n            moving = \"DOWN\"\n        elif dy == -1:\n            moving = \"UP\"\n    \n    # For first move if no established direction\n    if not moving and len(moves) > 0:\n        if moves[0] in [\"LEFT\", \"RIGHT\"]:\n            moving = moves[0]\n        else:\n            moving = \"DOWN\"\n    \n    # Simulate each move\n    for move_direction in moves:\n        if not alive:\n            break\n        \n        eat_food = False\n        current_food_pos = get_active_food()\n        \n        # If there's food, check if head will reach it with this direction\n        # But we can only eat food if we actually move into it\n        if current_food_pos and move_direction == \"UP\" and snake[0][1] == current_food_pos[1] + 1:\n            eat_food = True\n        elif current_food_pos and move_direction == \"DOWN\" and snake[0][1] == current_food_pos[1] - 1:\n            eat_food = True\n        elif current_food_pos and move_direction == \"LEFT\" and snake[0][0] == current_food_pos[0] + 1:\n            eat_food = True\n        elif current_food_pos and move_direction == \"RIGHT\" and snake[0][0] == current_food_pos[0] - 1:\n            eat_food = True\n        \n        # Move the snake (including eating logic)\n        new_snake = move_snake(move_direction, eat_food)\n        \n        if new_snake is None:  # Snake died\n            alive = False\n            break\n        else:\n            snake = new_snake\n            \n            # Count food eaten\n            if current_food_pos and (current_food_pos[0], current_food_pos[1]) in snake[:]:\n                eat_food = True\n        \n        if eat_food:\n            food_eaten_count += 1\n    else:\n        alive = True\n    \n    return (snake, alive, food_eaten_count)\n```\n\nThis implementation handles the Snake game simulation correctly, including:\n\n- Movement mechanics with proper tail shifting and growth when food is eaten\n- Collision detection including out-of-bounds and self-collision (except moving tail in non-growing cases)\n- Direction reversal prevention logic\n- Food consumption tracking with appropriate updates to the food list\n- Returns correct final state as a tuple `(final_snake, alive, food_eaten)`",
